---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import Fact from '../components/Fact.astro';
import { legal } from '../lib/legal';

const contents: [string, string][] = [
  ['about', 'About these terms'],
  ['purpose', 'What this website is for'],
  ['use', 'Using the website'],
  ['ownership', 'Content and ownership'],
  ['engagements', 'Inquiries, quotes and services'],
  ['results', 'No guaranteed results'],
  ['examples', 'Case studies, examples and testimonials'],
  ['third-parties', 'Third-party platforms and links'],
  ['disclaimer', 'Website information and availability'],
  ['liability', 'Limitation of liability'],
  ['law', 'Governing law'],
  ['changes', 'Changes to these terms'],
  ['contact', 'Contact us'],
];
---
<Base
  path="/terms-and-conditions"
  title="Terms & Conditions | VLORE"
  description="Terms for using the VLORE website: permitted use, content ownership, third-party links, and how quotes and services are governed by a separate written agreement."
  breadcrumb={[{ name: 'Terms & Conditions', path: '/terms-and-conditions' }]}
  page="inner"
  ctaHref="/contact"
>
  <link slot="head" rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/legal.css"/>
<LegalPage eyebrow="Legal" title="Terms & Conditions" effective="termsEffectiveDate" contents={contents}>

<h2 id="about">About these terms</h2>
<p>These terms apply to your use of vlore.ca (the “website”), operated by <Fact name="legalName" />, doing business as {legal.operatingName} (“VLORE”, “we”, “us”), of <Fact name="mailingAddress" />. By using the website, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the website.</p>
<p>These terms cover the website only. They are not a contract for marketing, design or development services; those are covered by a separate agreement (see <a href="#engagements">Inquiries, quotes and services</a>). How we handle personal information is explained in our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

<h2 id="purpose">What this website is for</h2>
<p>The website gives general information about VLORE and our services, shows examples of our work, and lets businesses contact us or request a free consultation. Its content is general information about marketing, branding and websites. It is not legal, financial, tax or other professional advice for your situation.</p>

<h2 id="use">Using the website</h2>
<p>You may use the website for lawful purposes, to learn about our services and to contact us. You agree not to:</p>
<ul>
<li>use the website in a way that breaks any law or infringes anyone’s rights;</li>
<li>submit false, misleading or someone else’s information, or send spam, automated or bulk submissions through our forms;</li>
<li>try to gain unauthorized access to the website, our systems or other people’s information, or test, probe or interfere with their security;</li>
<li>introduce malware or do anything that disrupts, overloads or impairs the website; or</li>
<li>copy, scrape or reuse the website’s content or design except as these terms allow.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="ownership">Content and ownership</h2>
<p>The text, design, graphics, logos, photographs and other content on the website are owned by us or used with permission, and are protected by copyright, trademark and other laws. You may view and print pages for your own information, and share links to them. Any other use, such as copying, modifying or republishing our content, requires our written permission.</p>
<p>Client names, logos, websites and work shown on the website belong to their respective owners and appear for portfolio purposes. Other trademarks mentioned, such as those of Google, Meta or Shopify, belong to their owners; their mention does not mean they endorse us.</p>

<h2 id="engagements">Inquiries, quotes and services</h2>
<p>Sending an inquiry or booking a free consultation does not create a contract or any obligation for either of us. Information on the website about our services, process or timelines is a general description, not an offer.</p>
<p>Any quote or proposal we give you is an estimate based on the information available at the time, unless it says otherwise. We provide services only under a separate written agreement or proposal that you and we both accept. That agreement sets out the scope, fees, timelines, ownership and other terms of the work, and it governs the services if it differs from anything on the website.</p>

<h2 id="results">No guaranteed results</h2>
<p>Marketing results depend on many things outside our control, including your market, competition, budget, offer, pricing, sales process, and the policies and algorithms of search engines and advertising platforms. Unless a signed agreement expressly says otherwise, we do not promise or guarantee any particular search ranking, traffic, number of leads, sales, revenue, return on ad spend or other business outcome.</p>

<h2 id="examples">Case studies, examples and testimonials</h2>
<p>Case studies, client examples and testimonials on the website describe the experience of specific clients in their own circumstances. They are not typical results or a promise of what you will achieve. Your results will vary.</p>

<h2 id="third-parties">Third-party platforms and links</h2>
<p>Much of our work relies on third-party platforms, such as search engines, advertising networks, social media, website and e-commerce platforms, email and CRM tools, and AI services. Those platforms set their own terms, fees, policies and approval rules, which can change without notice. We are not responsible for a third party’s decisions, outages or policy changes, but this does not limit our responsibility for our own acts or omissions.</p>
<p>The website links to other websites, including client websites and social media. We do not control those websites and are not responsible for their content or practices.</p>

<h2 id="disclaimer">Website information and availability</h2>
<p>We try to keep the website accurate and available, but we do not guarantee that its content is complete, current or error-free, or that the website will always be available or free of viruses or other harmful components. To the extent permitted by law, the website and its content are provided “as is” and “as available”, without warranties of any kind, whether express or implied.</p>

<h2 id="liability">Limitation of liability</h2>
<p>To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any indirect, incidental, special or consequential loss, or for any loss of profits, revenue, data or business opportunity, arising from your use of, or inability to use, the website or its content.</p>
<p>Nothing in these terms excludes or limits any liability, right or remedy that cannot be excluded or limited under applicable law. Our liability for services we provide is governed by the agreement for those services, not by these terms.</p>

<h2 id="law">Governing law</h2>
<p>These terms are governed by the laws of the Province of Ontario and the federal laws of Canada that apply there. <Fact todo="LAWYER: confirm whether to add a choice of courts (e.g. Ontario courts) clause" /> This does not take away any protection you are entitled to under the mandatory laws of the place where you live.</p>

<h2 id="changes">Changes to these terms</h2>
<p>We may update these terms from time to time. The updated version will be posted on this page with a new effective date and applies to your use of the website from that date.</p>

<h2 id="contact">Contact us</h2>
<address>
<Fact name="legalName" />, doing business as {legal.operatingName}<br/>
<Fact name="mailingAddress" /><br/>
<a href={`mailto:${legal.privacyEmail}`}>{legal.privacyEmail}</a>
</address>

</LegalPage>
</Base>
